## cmesh BYOL hardening — /etc/audit/rules.d/99-cmesh-immutable.rules
## Must sort last. -e 2 locks the ruleset: no process, root included, can change or
## disable auditing until the next reboot. Changing rules therefore means editing
## rules.d and rebooting; cmesh-byol-harden says so when it hits the lock.
-e 2
